{"text": "April 10, 1986\n\nTo: Distribution\n\u2018FROM: R. J. Harden\n\nSUBJECT: PRODUCT PERFORMANCE SUMMARY - MARCH, 1986\n\nAttached is a summary of RJRT product performance versus competition, among\nboth target competitive and franchise smokers, for March, 1986 (Attachment 1).\nProvided in this summary is a comparison to March, 1985, performance,\n\u2018Also attached are monthly tracking of competitive product performance for each\nRIRT brand style (Attachment 2) and a listing of current RJRT product per-\nformance by brand style among target competitive and franchise smoker groups\n(Attachment 3).\n\nLastly, attached are product test results received during March in three\ncategories: Product Consistency (Attachment 5), Product Improvement\n(Attachment 6) and Product Translation (Attachment 7).\n\nBelow highlights the attached results.\n\nCompetitive Performance\n\nAmong target competitive smokers, the following changes in performance\noccurred relative to performance in March, 1985. The percentage of RJRT\nvolume in products with superior performance versus competition increased from H]\n4% to 15% due mainly to the improved performance of SALEM Lights 85 and 100,\n\u2018Also, the percentage of RJRT volume in products with inferior performance\nincreased from 8% to 16% mainly because of the decline in performance for\nCAMEL Lighte 85, CAMEL Filter 85, and WINSTON Lights 100, .\n\nFor franchise smokers, March, 1986, data shows an increase in the percentage\nof RJRT volume in products with an inferior performance from 0% to 6% becaus\nof a elip in performance by WINSTON 100.\n\n2625 LtSOS",
